PART 1. PRODUCT IDENTITY

1.1. Name and slogan

Use a temporary product name: APEX.

Main slogan:

“Education is not preparation for life; education is life itself””

Supporting message:

“Discover your talent. Develop your skills. Make your work significant.”

1.2. Product philosophy

The platform is built around three main stages:

1. DISCOVER — explore academic fields, educational opportunities, programs, competitions, scholarships, and challenges.
2. DEVELOP — build skills, follow a personalized growth plan, and collect evidence of achievements.
3. DISCOURSE — submit work to professors, receive feedback, and share achievements with universities.

The platform must not replace the student’s effort or independent thinking.

AI is a mentor and assistant, not an automatic decision-maker.

Core principle:

“AI doesn’t replace student effort. It amplifies student potential.”

AI can organize information, suggest opportunities, ask questions, explain requirements, and provide feedback. Students remain responsible for their decisions, applications, academic work, and achievements.

PART 2. DESIGN SYSTEM AND VISUAL IDENTITY

2.1. Overall aesthetic

Create a beautiful, modern, premium-looking interface.

Visual direction:

* Fresh academic aesthetic.
* Editorial minimalism.
* Modern technology.
* Soft pastel colors.
* Clean white backgrounds.
* Elegant typography.
* Subtle futuristic details.

The website should look like a professionally designed international EdTech startup, not a generic AI-generated dashboard.

It should feel intelligent, welcoming, creative, and trustworthy.

2.2. Color palette

Use these exact colors as the starting design system:

* White: #FFFFFF — primary background.
* Matcha Green: #B7E6A5 — primary accent.
* Soft Pink: #F6C9D5 — secondary accent.
* Sage Green: #F3F7F0 — secondary background.
* Dark Text: #26332D — primary typography.
* Muted Text: #78847B — secondary typography.
* Light Border: #E7ECE6 — dividers and card borders.

Color distribution:

* 65–75% white and very light backgrounds.
* Matcha green for primary buttons, active navigation, progress indicators, and important highlights.
* Soft pink for secondary cards, illustrations, badges, and decorative details.
* Sage green for selected sections and subtle card backgrounds.
* Dark charcoal for readable text.

Do not use pink and green everywhere. Keep the interface balanced and professional.

2.3. Typography

Use a combination of:

* An elegant, expressive heading font.
* A clean, modern sans-serif font for body text and interface elements.

Typography should have a clear hierarchy:

* Large editorial headlines on the landing page.
* Medium section headings.
* Compact but readable dashboard labels.
* Consistent text sizes and spacing.

2.4. UI components

Use:

* Rounded cards with consistent corner radii.
* Thin borders.
* Very subtle shadows.
* Beautiful, minimal icons.
* Clear buttons with visible hover and active states.
* Consistent spacing.
* Elegant progress bars.
* Small status badges.
* Smooth page transitions.
* Subtle animations when cards appear.
* Thoughtful empty states and loading states.

Avoid:

* Excessive gradients.
* Neon colors.
* Heavy shadows.
* Crowded dashboards.
* Unnecessary decorative elements.
* Too many different card styles.

Make the entire platform responsive for desktop, tablet, and mobile.

